# desk.ps2 - the session software/desk/bench/run-v3desk.sh drives the desktop with.
#
# ⭐ SCREEN COORDINATES, Y DOWN (software/emu/ps2script.h).  Time zero is
# PS2_SCRIPT_GATE: the moment `desk` has printed DESK-READY on the console,
# which is after its first full paint - so nothing here races the drawing.
#
# ⚠ `origin` MUST BE desk.asm's GEO.ORGX/GEO.ORGY.  desk issues one PutGC at
# start-up and never another (its header says why), so this is where the
# machine's mouse really is; get it wrong and every coordinate below is off
# by the difference and still self-consistent.
origin 320 240
gap 120                     # a click's down-to-up: three passes of a 60 Hz loop

# --- 1  the bar, and the pull-down --------------------------------------
at 1.500    move to 100 8   # over the Applications title
+0.700      click left      # C0: the menu comes down
+0.900      move to 168 32  # H: item 0, Paint
+0.900      move to 168 52  # H: item 1, Monsterland - a DIFFERENT item
+0.900      move to 168 72  # H: item 2, Stardew - a THIRD item, and it
#                             was the greyed one until 2026-09-21
+0.900      move to 500 300 # off the menu, and off the pull-down's rectangle
+0.700      click left      # C1: dismissed, and what was under it comes back

# --- 2  the launcher ----------------------------------------------------
# ⛔ SIX SECONDS AFTER THE DISMISSAL, AND IT IS MEASURED, NOT SLACK.  Shutting
# a menu repaints the WHOLE desktop (desk.asm's DrawAll), and `desk` samples
# the button once a loop pass - so a click that lands inside that repaint is
# not late, it is GONE, exactly as files.ps2's header records for the file
# manager.  ⚠ 1.400 was enough for six desktop icons and is not enough for
# ELEVEN: on 2026-09-22 C2 arrived 2.24 s after C1, the menu never reopened,
# and seven claims failed describing a desktop that was simply still drawing.
+6.000      move to 100 8
+0.700      click left      # C2: open again
+0.900      move to 168 32  # Paint
+0.700      click left      # C3: ⭐ forks v3paint off /SD0/CMDS

# --- 3  the fourth item, whose module this card does not carry ----------
# ⚠ ABSOLUTE, not relative: everything between here and C3 is the child's -
# and how long it takes is not this script's business.
# ⛔ 75, NOT 60, AND IT IS MEASURED (2026-09-22).  checkdesk.py reports the
# child's own frames: C3 clicked at 45.8 s, Paint's page was on the card from
# 70.4 s to 91.2 s and the desktop was back at 92.1 - ⭐ FORTY-SIX SECONDS
# from the click, where the note below recorded ~26 when the desktop had six
# icons.  Most of it is the child (the fork, the DWSet, and 33 KB of stream
# through the toolbox), not the repaint.  60 put C4 at 91.3 s, INSIDE Paint's
# last second, and five claims failed describing a desktop that was busy.
at 75.000   move to 100 8
+0.700      click left      # C4
+0.900      move to 168 72  # Stardew (item 2 since Pinball and Zelda left the menu)
+0.700      click left      # C5: ⭐ asks for the launch by name.  The module
#                             is not on this bench's card, so F$Fork fails

# --- 4  quit, through the menu that offers it ---------------------------
# ⛔ ABSOLUTE, AND TWENTY-SEVEN SECONDS AFTER C5, which is not slack: it is
# measured.  A.Run gives the window up with DWEnd, the child DWSets a screen
# of its own, and when it returns `desk` DWSets ITS screen again and repaints
# from its display list - and every one of those goes through CoArm's toolbox
# escapes.  The recording says the card showed the child's 640 x 400 from
# 96.2 s to 114.4 s even though `stardew` only got as far as reporting that
# its world file is missing: ⭐ THE DESKTOP IS DEAF FOR ~26 s AFTER A LAUNCH
# WHATEVER THE CHILD DOES (software/desk/docs/boot-and-desktop.md §5 item 4).  A relative
# +1.400 here put C6 inside that window and the Quit was never seen.
at 110.000  move to 30 8    # the Desk title
+0.700      click left      # C6
+0.900      move to 60 52   # Quit
+0.700      click left      # C7: desk exits, and the shell prompt comes back
